      "message": "[From Jetski review] On macOS (`platform.is_darwin()`), `get_packages()` only downloads host clang and does not download a `sysroot` package, so `cipd_dir / \u0027sysroot\u0027` does not exist. Passing `--sysroot\u003d{sysroot}` unconditionally here will break local builds on macOS (note that `cq_mac` doesn\u0027t catch this because `infra/recipes/gn.py` sets `CXX` in the environment, bypassing this `elif` branch).\n\nShould `cflags.append(f\u0027--sysroot\u003d{sysroot}\u0027)` and `ldflags.append(f\u0027--sysroot\u003d{sysroot}\u0027)` be guarded by `if platform.is_linux():`? (Also nit on line 463: `hermetic sysroots` -\u003e `hermetic clang`).",
